From 8bee1097549ff10e2413d8fe6de3956f1dcff864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Revulate <76570121+Revulate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:59:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gpui): keep a reused cached view's accessibility nodes

`A11y::begin_frame` clears the node tree, node bounds, focus
registrations and action listeners every frame, and they are only
rebuilt by `Drawable::prepaint` (nodes, bounds), `Interactivity::prepaint`
(focus) and `Interactivity::paint` (action listeners). A cached view
whose prepaint and paint are reused skips all of that for its subtree,
and `Window::reuse_prepaint` replayed hitboxes, tooltips, element states,
line layouts and the dispatch subtree but nothing for accessibility. On
any frame where a cached view was reused, its whole subtree vanished from
the tree sent to the platform, along with its focus and live regions,
and came back on the next frame that re-rendered it. Apps that cache
large views (chat lists, roots, bars) dropped most of their tree on
ordinary frames.

The finished nodes of a frame are now kept until the next frame instead
of being moved into the `TreeUpdate`, together with the stack depth at
which each node was attached. `PrepaintStateIndex` records the node
count and stack depth, so a view's prepaint range also covers the nodes
its subtree finished, which are contiguous because every node a subtree
pushes is popped before its prepaint returns. `reuse_prepaint` replays
that range through `A11y::reuse_nodes`:

- the nodes move over unchanged (their child lists only name nodes of
  the same subtree), and the ones that were children of the subtree's
  parent are attached to the current parent, at the current depth;
- node bounds and focus registrations are copied from the previous
  frame's maps, which `begin_frame` now keeps aside until `end_frame`
  instead of clearing;
- action listeners are boxed closures and can't be cloned, so they are
  moved out of the previous frame's map, as reused mouse listeners are
  moved out of the rendered frame; the reused paint never registers
  them again;
- the focused node is restored when its focus handle is still the
  window's focus, and the active descendant when the focused node is
  still its ancestor, since the elements that report both are skipped.

Nothing changes while accessibility is inactive: prepaint indices hold
zeros, `reuse_prepaint` skips the replay, and a frame drawn inactive
drops any kept tree. The first active frame after that has nothing to
replay from, so it renders every view (the activation callback already
requests a refresh, but a frame can be drawn before it runs). While
active, each frame clones its node list once, for the next frame.

New unit tests cover replay under a different parent and depth, replay
of an already replayed range, the moved focus, bounds and listeners, and
the release. `reused_cached_view_keeps_its_nodes` draws a window whose
root re-renders around a reused cached view with accessibility active
and checks `Window::debug_a11y_tree_json`; it fails without the replay.

